= Tool use in artificial intelligence — Simple =

'''Tool use''' means an AI system can call something outside itself to help complete a task.

For example, it might use:

* a calculator;
* a search engine;
* a database;
* a program;
* an API;
* a browser.

Using a tool involves more than knowing the tool exists.

The system may need to choose the right tool, give it the right inputs, read the result, and decide what to do next.

One tool call does not automatically make a system an AI agent.

